{
  "scenario_id": "sim-cold-chain-compressor-failover-repair",
  "title": "Cold chain: compressor failover ladder and repair",
  "description": "One refrigeration rack driven through the full failover ladder: a lone compressor (N) fails and the rack is lost; a standby is added (N -> N+1) and the still-faulted primary is absorbed so service returns before any repair; the repair itself is then invisible to service loss; a condenser fault (no redundancy anywhere on its path) drops the rack again and its repair restores it. Adjudicates Category 1 (failover semantics under N vs N+1) and Category 2 (multi-step fault -> dependent loss -> restore) for the cold-chain beachhead.",
